@startuml API Gateway Sequence Diagram
!theme plain
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

title API Gateway — Sequence Diagram (caa 30 March 2026)

actor Client
participant "API Gateway" as GW
participant "Firebase Auth" as FA
database "redis-auth" as RA
database "redis-sessions" as RS
participant "Question Service" as QS
participant "Upstream Service" as US

== Token Verification (all protected routes) ==

Client -> GW: Any request\nAuthorization: Bearer <token>
GW -> FA: verify_id_token(token)

alt Token invalid / expired
    FA --> GW: Exception
    GW --> Client: 401 "Auth Failed: ..."
else Token valid
    FA --> GW: {uid, role, iat}
    GW -> RA: EXISTS invalidated_user:{uid}
    alt User deleted
        RA --> GW: true
        GW --> Client: 401 "ACCOUNT_DELETED"
    else
        GW -> RA: GET stale_claims:{uid}
        alt Claims stale (iat <= stale_ts)
            RA --> GW: timestamp
            GW --> Client: 403 "TOKEN_STALE"
        else Checks pass
            note over GW: Inject X-User-Id and X-User-Role headers\nForward to upstream service
        end
    end
end

note over GW: If redis-auth is unreachable, checks are\nskipped (fail-open) and request proceeds.

== Session Initialisation (POST /session/init) ==

note over Client, RS: Both matched users call this endpoint concurrently.\nLeader election via Redis SETNX ensures one session is created.

Client -> GW: POST /session/init\nAuthorization: Bearer <token>\n{peer_id, topic, difficulty}
GW -> FA: verify_id_token(token)
FA --> GW: {uid}

GW -> RS: SETNX lock:match:{userA}:{userB} = <uuid>

alt Leader (SETNX returned true)
    GW -> RS: EXPIRE lock:match:{userA}:{userB} 5s
    GW -> QS: GET /question/?topic=...&difficulty=...
    QS --> GW: {question_id}
    GW -> RS: SETEX session:{room_id}:meta 7200 {user1,user2,topic,difficulty,questionId}
    GW -> RS: SETEX active_session:{userA} 7200 {room_id}
    GW -> RS: SETEX active_session:{userB} 7200 {room_id}
    GW --> Client: 200 {room_id}
else Follower (SETNX returned false)
    GW -> RS: GET lock:match:{userA}:{userB}
    RS --> GW: room_id
    loop Poll until meta written (max 10s)
        GW -> RS: GET session:{room_id}:meta
        RS --> GW: meta or nil
    end
    GW --> Client: 200 {room_id}
end

== Proxy — Authenticated Request ==

Client -> GW: <METHOD> /<service>/...\nAuthorization: Bearer <token>
note over GW: Token verified (see above)
GW -> US: Forward request\nX-User-Id: {uid}\nX-User-Role: {role}\n(Authorization header stripped)
US --> GW: Response
note over GW: Strip upstream CORS headers\n(nginx owns CORS for /api/ requests)
GW --> Client: Upstream response

== Proxy — Public Request ==

note over GW: Public routes: POST /users, GET /users/lookup/{username}

Client -> GW: POST /users OR GET /users/lookup/{username}
GW -> US: Forward request (no auth headers injected)
US --> GW: Response
GW --> Client: Upstream response

@enduml
